  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x6B4A" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration Target - Running [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x171C2; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 15 duration target of the VVEL selector: the normal running mode above idle without a hot-intake or throttled request. The resolver interpolates it by engine speed and scales the count by the float literal 0.005 before the selector publishes the command. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0x171c2 bound to accessor 0x5f468 through literal 0x5f764, accessor 0x5fd88 through literal 0x5fe5c. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*0.005 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x/0.005. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:409-441, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:478-505, vvel_duration_running_axis/axis. The encoded arithmetic factor is not the physical duration unit. The float literal is a binary value described by its nominal decimal factor, not a measurement of degrees. The returned table quantity is distinct from its axis-coordinate quantity and from the paired command-word domain. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the resolver FUN_0005F468 at callsite 0x5F5DE and by FUN_0005FD88 through the 16-point uint16 wrapper 0x2893C; the 0.005 factor is the float literal 0x3BA3D70A at 0x5F768. Six of the sixteen stock points differ from the JK78C curve 0x00016BB4 at the same axis; the unit of the scaled duration is a vendor-catalog candidate. 1ND3B shares the 1ND0A code layout and its stock bytes at this address. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
