    <title>VVEL Shaft Angle Limit - Engine Speed [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x166B8; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Engine-speed curve of the shaft-angle bound applied in the task before the command conversion. Values are in the shaft-angle domain of axis 0x00015C02. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0x166b8 bound to accessor 0x5e2a0 through literal 0x5e5a4. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x/512 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x*512. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:491-499, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:525-530, vvel_shaft_angle_axis/axis, vvel_command_shaft_angle/tbl. A shared integer domain, maximum, subtraction, absolute-value correction or word bound preserves count arithmetic. None independently fixes 512 counts per physical degree. An RPM or CVTC input grid cannot establish the returned shaft-coordinate unit. The upstream coordinate scale itself has no physical grounding in the finite sources. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the task FUN_0005E2A0 at callsite 0x5E378 through the 8-point uint16 wrapper 0x28910. Stock bytes are identical to JK78C 0x000160BA. 1ND3B shares the 1ND0A code layout and its stock bytes at this address. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
