  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x107F" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration Target - Hot Intake Idle, Knock [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0xE7C8; 8 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 13 duration surface of the VVEL selector: hot-intake idle with the high-detonation state set. Stock values are 1000 = 50.0 at every cell. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0xe7c8 bound to accessor 0x5f468 through literal 0x5f7a8, accessor 0x70514 through literal 0x712a4. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*0.05 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x/0.05. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:409-441, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:478-505. A knock-state selector and identical stock bytes do not establish physical duration degrees. The returned table quantity is distinct from its axis-coordinate quantity and from the paired command-word domain. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the resolver FUN_0005F468 at callsite 0x5F688 through the 8x8 uint16 wrapper 0x28674 with the same byte coordinates and axes as the mode 12 surface 0x0000E748, and by FUN_00070514 at 0x7108E and 0x7115A. 1ND3B shares the 1ND0A code layout and its stock bytes at this address. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
