  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xA86C" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration Target - Cold [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x17062; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 3 duration target of the VVEL selector: the cold branch. Interpolated by a coolant-coded byte and scaled by 0.05. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0x17062 bound to accessor 0x5f468 through literal 0x5f7b4. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*0.05 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x/0.05. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:409-441, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:478-505. The coolant-coordinate proof does not prove the duration output unit. The returned table quantity is distinct from its axis-coordinate quantity and from the paired command-word domain. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the resolver FUN_0005F468 at callsite 0x5F6D2 through the 8-point uint16 wrapper 0x28910 with its own literal pool words for the curve and the axis. Stock bytes are identical to JK78C 0x00016A54. 1ND3B shares the 1ND0A code layout and its stock bytes at this address. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="25" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0" flags="0x0">
