    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x132450; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. Coolant-indexed lower/full-restore RPM threshold in FUN 00050018. At speed count below 4 it is the lower boundary for class 3. At speed count 4 or above every branch reachable under the stock compile-time flags returns class 3 at or below the effective lower threshold and class 0 only strictly above it. Common-definition Map 3 storage is projected from 0x141D4. Stock firmware does not reference this allocated storage; it becomes runtime-active only with the project map-switching patch. The adjusted result is stored in ffff16aa after coolant floors, runtime offsets, and a conditional minimum of 48 counts or 1200 RPM. Exact stock moving branches ignore upper/intermediate table 0001298c. The target-vehicle capture selected only moving samples, retained stock 000126e4/00012718, changed both restore tables, and eliminated the full 0x3f inhibit mask below 5000 RPM. Because 0001298c is not compared on that branch, this hardware result isolates 00012818 as the operational moving veto. Equality remains class 3, so a raw value of 200 vetoes through exactly 5000 RPM in the quantized coordinate and class 0 begins only above it. Result disposition: inline_comparison. Definition address projected from JK08A 00012818 through JK08A-1ND.definition-addresses.csv: homologous restore coordinator preserves the lower table role and exact table bytes. Static diagnostic context: Engine Coolant Temperature [code, homologous_community, via map evidence: indexed_by].</description>
