  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x7954" flags="0x0">
    <title>Map 5 - Fuel Compensation - Main - Alternate [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x133000; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Alternate multiplicative fuel-correction surface. It shares the index byte, both axes, and the interpolator of the projected default surface, and the downstream state selector reads it in place of that surface. The proposed raw-128 unity normalization has no independent reference. Common-definition Map 5 storage is projected from 0xA2C0. Stock firmware does not reference this allocated storage; it becomes runtime-active only with the project map-switching patch. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0xa2c0 bound to accessor 0x30810 through literal 0x31164, accessor 0x44f1c through literal 0x454f8. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*0.78125 %; proposed editor-grid inverse x/0.78125. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK08A.findings.csv:57, fuel_compensation_main/tbl. The alternate role and common channel supply a bounded candidate interpretation, not code-level physical unity. The default registry record does not name the alternate table. It must not be copied as if it did. No engine-bank identity follows from the table pair. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: The two 16x16 surfaces are read with the same index byte, the same axis pair, and the same interpolator in both accessors, so neither surface carries an engine-bank identity. The accessors publish four parallel compensation channels and the consumer selects one by a state code, then crossfades the value of the current state with the value of the previous state by a normalized progress weight where 0x8000 is 1.0. The default arm of that selector reads the projected canonical surface; this table is the arm the state code selects instead. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
